{"episode_view":{"attempts_remaining":8,"attempts_used":2,"case":{"background":"Monochromatic light illuminates a clean cathode in a vacuum phototube. Vary frequency and the absorbed photon rate, then use stopping potential and saturation current to explain when and how electrons are emitted.","budget":10,"case_id":"phototube.response.world_a","confidence_threshold":0.9,"initial_observations":["Some illumination settings produce no measurable photocurrent.","When electrons are emitted, a reverse voltage can stop the current."],"max_hypotheses":6,"resources":{"controls":[{"allowed_values":[],"description":"Frequency of monochromatic incident light.","maximum":1000.0,"minimum":400.0,"name":"frequency_thz","unit":"THz"},{"allowed_values":[],"description":"Absorbed photon rate at the cathode relative to the reference setting.","maximum":2.0,"minimum":0.1,"name":"absorbed_photon_flux_relative","unit":"relative"}],"instruments":[{"controls":["frequency_thz","absorbed_photon_flux_relative"],"description":"A clean-cathode vacuum phototube with monochromatic illumination and electrical meters.","name":"vacuum_phototube","readouts":["stopping_potential_v","saturation_current_ua"]}],"max_replicates":15,"notes":["The cathode remains clean and unchanged across experiments.","When a work function is reported in volts, it denotes the energy divided by elementary charge.","The photon-flux control is absorbed photon rate, not optical power or irradiance.","Above threshold, the ideal cathode has frequency-independent quantum yield and the saturation circuit collects every emitted electron.","Zero current and stopping potential mean no emitted electrons.","FinalSubmission.model must equal 'einstein_photoelectric_law'. FinalSubmission.parameters must contain exactly h_over_e_v_s, work_function_equivalent_v, reference_saturation_current_ua. Candidate law: excess_voltage = h_over_e_v_s*frequency_thz*1e12 - work_function_equivalent_v; stopping_potential_v=max(0,excess_voltage); current is zero for excess_voltage<=0 and otherwise reference_saturation_current_ua*absorbed_photon_flux_relative."],"readouts":[{"description":"Reverse-potential magnitude needed to reduce photocurrent to zero.","name":"stopping_potential_v","resolution":0.01,"unit":"V"},{"description":"Saturation photocurrent with all emitted electrons collected.","name":"saturation_current_ua","resolution":0.02,"unit":"uA"}]},"title":"Identify the phototube frequency-photon-flux response","track":"identification"},"turns":[{"attempt_index":1,"portfolio":{"hypotheses":[{"confidence":0.5,"hypothesis_id":"H1","statement":"The photoelectric effect follows Einstein's law with a threshold frequency; stopping potential increases linearly with frequency above threshold, and saturation current is proportional to absorbed photon flux."},{"confidence":0.3,"hypothesis_id":"H2","statement":"Photocurrent depends only on light intensity (photon flux), not frequency; higher flux always produces current regardless of frequency."},{"confidence":0.2,"hypothesis_id":"H3","statement":"There is a minimum photon flux required for emission, and above that flux, current is independent of frequency."}]},"proposal":{"apparatus":"vacuum_phototube","controls":{"absorbed_photon_flux_relative":1.0,"frequency_thz":600.0},"forecasts":{"H1":{"saturation_current_ua":10.0,"stopping_potential_v":1.0},"H2":{"saturation_current_ua":10.0,"stopping_potential_v":0.5},"H3":{"saturation_current_ua":0.0,"stopping_potential_v":0.0}},"intent":"Test the frequency dependence of the photoelectric effect by measuring stopping potential and saturation current at two different frequencies while holding photon flux constant.","readouts":["stopping_potential_v","saturation_current_ua"],"replicates":3},"response":{"evidence":{"measurements":{"saturation_current_ua":3.0,"stopping_potential_v":0.2},"message":"The apparatus reports the deterministic mean of 3 replicate(s).","uncertainty":{"saturation_current_ua":"+/- 0.01 uA (rounding interval)","stopping_potential_v":"+/- 0.005 V (rounding interval)"},"units":{"saturation_current_ua":"uA","stopping_potential_v":"V"}},"message":"The apparatus reports the deterministic mean of 3 replicate(s).","status":"VALID"},"turn_index":1},{"attempt_index":2,"portfolio":{"hypotheses":[{"confidence":0.85,"hypothesis_id":"H1","statement":"The photoelectric effect follows Einstein's law with a threshold frequency; stopping potential increases linearly with frequency above threshold, and saturation current is proportional to absorbed photon flux."},{"confidence":0.05,"hypothesis_id":"H2","statement":"Photocurrent depends only on light intensity (photon flux), not frequency; higher flux always produces current regardless of frequency."},{"confidence":0.05,"hypothesis_id":"H3","statement":"There is a minimum photon flux required for emission, and above that flux, current is independent of frequency."},{"confidence":0.05,"hypothesis_id":"H4","statement":"Stopping potential increases linearly with frequency above threshold, but saturation current depends on both flux and a frequency-dependent quantum efficiency."}]},"proposal":{"apparatus":"vacuum_phototube","controls":{"absorbed_photon_flux_relative":1.0,"frequency_thz":800.0},"forecasts":{"H1":{"saturation_current_ua":3.0,"stopping_potential_v":1.03},"H2":{"saturation_current_ua":3.0,"stopping_potential_v":0.5},"H3":{"saturation_current_ua":0.0,"stopping_potential_v":0.0},"H4":{"saturation_current_ua":4.0,"stopping_potential_v":1.03}},"intent":"Measure stopping potential and saturation current at a second, higher frequency with the same photon flux to estimate the slope of stopping potential vs frequency and test flux-scaling of saturation current.","readouts":["stopping_potential_v","saturation_current_ua"],"replicates":3},"response":{"evidence":{"measurements":{"saturation_current_ua":3.0,"stopping_potential_v":1.03},"message":"The apparatus reports the deterministic mean of 3 replicate(s).","uncertainty":{"saturation_current_ua":"+/- 0.01 uA (rounding interval)","stopping_potential_v":"+/- 0.005 V (rounding interval)"},"units":{"saturation_current_ua":"uA","stopping_potential_v":"V"}},"message":"The apparatus reports the deterministic mean of 3 replicate(s).","status":"VALID"},"turn_index":2}],"wire_schema":"role_benchmark.episode_view"},"repair":{"instruction":"Generate exactly one valid action for the same episode view. You received no Oracle response or evidence between calls. This is a second generation and may differ semantically.","invalid_output":"{
